# How git should treat the bytes in this repository.
#
# Three jobs: keep line endings from becoming a diff, keep resolver output out
# of review and out of GitHub's language stats, and give git the hunk-header
# rules that make a diff readable.
#
# NOT here on purpose: `export-ignore`. It would trim files out of the tarball
# GitHub generates for a tag, and that tarball is what a downstream `zig fetch`
# hashes - the url+hash pin in a consumer's `build.zig.zon` is a hash of those
# bytes. Excluding anything to save someone a download would invalidate every
# pin that already exists. What ships in the Zig package is already decided,
# deliberately and reviewably, by `.paths` in build.zig.zon.

# ── Line endings ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Normalize on commit, LF in the working tree on every platform. This face
# re-reads current bytes and re-finds a phrase in them exactly; a checkout that
# silently introduced CRLF would change the bytes a provenance answer is
# verified against, which is the one thing this package promises not to do.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ── Generated ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lockfiles: resolver output. Reviewed as a fact ("this version moved"), never
# read line by line.
*.lock  linguist-generated -diff

# Anything projected from contract/*.toml, should a generator ever land its
# output in the tree rather than checking it. Nothing matches today; the rule
# is here so that the day one does, the diff worth reading is still the
# contract's.
*.gen.zig      linguist-generated
schema.gen.*   linguist-generated

# NOT marked, because they are not written here: `zig build` stages the sibling
# headers (irgx.h, gist.h) beside this package's own at install time. They
# belong to the packages that declare them and are never committed.

# ── Diff drivers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Git ships hunk-header patterns for these; naming them here is what makes
# `@@ ... fn whatever` appear above a hunk instead of a bare line number.
*.go  diff=golang
*.py  diff=python
*.rs  diff=rust
*.h   diff=cpp
*.md  diff=markdown

# Zig has no built-in driver. The attribute is inert until the pattern exists
# in your own git config; CONTRIBUTING.md has the one-line command, and without
# it this line simply falls back to git's default behaviour.
*.zig diff=zig

# ── Merge ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The changelog is append-at-the-top and assembled by towncrier. Two branches
# adding release sections conflict textually while agreeing semantically; a
# union merge keeps both and lets the next `towncrier build` sort it out.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
